Write a JavaScript code to construct a sentence where all words start with the same letter. The letter should be the first letter of the first word.
Example:
Input : arr = {“hello”, “world”, “how”, “are”, “you”}
Output : “ahehowaryou”
Input : arr = {“hello”, “w”, “h”, “o”, “w”, “o”, “r”, “l”, “d”}
Output : “whworldrld”

Solution:
The idea is to take the first word of given array and check if it is a palindrome or not.
If it is a palindrome, then it is the first word of the sentence. A palindrome word is a word that is spelled the same way backwards as it is forwards.
If not, then we loop through all words of the given array and check if current word is palindrome. If it is, then it is the second word of the sentence. If not, then we again loop through all words and find the third word and so on.
We add the first word in the result.
Finally, we add the last word of the result in the result.
Below is the implementation of the above approach:

## C++

