@Jim - I don't have a reference for it, but I'm pretty sure it's a compound verb. "Scan" is a transitive verb, meaning that it requires a direct object. A compound verb has two parts, both of which are verbs, each of which has its own object. "Scan the barcode" is the equivalent of "scan something with a barcode scanner" in which "scan" is one verb and "the barcode" is the direct object. –  Cascabel Mar 30 '18 at 6:51
