The phrase "to scan" can be used in any of these ways:
  1. to scan a barcode using a barcode scanner or other device
  2. to use a barcode scanner or other device to scan a barcode
  3. to use a barcode scanner or other device to scan a barcode and then do something with the scanned barcode (e.g., look up the book on Amazon or Goodreads)
I would say that the phrase "to scan" is commonly used in the first two ways.
The phrase "to scan a barcode" is less common, and I would say that it is only used in way 2 above. I don’t think that it would sound right to me to use it in way 3.
